# Component colocation

Root `components/` holds **only** UI shared across the application, grouped by role:

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `ui/` | Design-system primitives |
| `layout/` | Shell + chrome used only by the store layout (header, footer, cart, chat, contact) |
| `cards/` | Shared entity cards (plant, blog) |
| `reviews/` | Shared review UI primitives |
| `forms/` | Shared form helpers |
| `system/` | App wiring (analytics, query provider, JSON-LD) |
| `feedback/` | Global status / error / not-found views |

If a module is only imported from `components/layout/**`, keep it under `components/layout/` (do not promote to a top-level folder).

Name shared UI for its role, not a single route (`CatalogList` not `PlantList` when used by plants + categories).

Route-specific or route-family UI belongs under that route’s private folder:

- `app/<route>/_components/` for a single route
- `app/[locale]/(store)/_components/<feature>/` when shared within the store group only (e.g. `catalog/`)

Do **not** add new homepage-, detail-, admin-, or checkout-only sections to root `components/`.
